# Lick: Pull-Offs (repertoire plan: st-lick-pull-off). An original lick in E minor pentatonic,
# open position (E G A B D). Three pull-offs to open strings: string 1 fret 3 to open (G to E),
# string 2 fret 3 to open (D to B), string 3 fret 2 to open (A to G). Pick only the fretted note;
# the finger plucks the open note as it leaves (fret 3 is finger 3, fret 2 is finger 2).
# Bars 1-4 come down the strings in pull-off pairs; bars 5-7 join a hammer-on and a pull-off
# into slow trills on strings 3, 2 and 1 (one pick for the whole bar); bar 8 walks down to an
# E minor chord. Notes on beats 1 and 3 are notes of Em7 (E G B D), or an A that pulls off to G.
title: Lick: Pull-Offs
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original lick
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: pull-off, hammer-on, trill, legato, minor pentatonic, lick
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: Em

track: Your lick
role: lead
